# goal-nudge-surface-starve: R22. Goal nudges emitted under the all-idle gate must still be
# surfaced by the orchestrator pump when a worker turns busy AFTER emission (the nudge's own
# requested action succeeding). Pre-R22 the pump's staleSurfaceReason goal-key agent_busy leg
# dropped them forever: notification.stale.suppressed site=orchestrator_pump.surface
# reason=agent_busy, mailbox.orchestrator_pump_stuck_escalated every tick, zero pi.sendMessage.
#
# Pattern 2 (seeded world + single-actor script) per .agents/skills/mock-llm-scenarios/SKILL.md:
# the launch script seeds the EXACT live-incident snapshot (2026-09-02T12:04:08Z) — worker-a
# runtimeStatus=tool_running with a fresh heartbeat, goal present, idle anchor BEFORE the nudge
# createdAt, and 3 goal nudges already emitted + durably queued (mailbox + message records,
# requiresAck, priority normal, keys goal:<gid>:nudge:idle-streak:1..3). Cross-process
# "worker turns busy mid-scenario" timing (Pattern 3) is deliberately avoided: it is the
# non-determinism this fixture must not have; the seeded snapshot is the deterministic proxy
# declared in the R22 plan §6. The engine (pump) runs for real on its watchdog tick: POST-R22
# the pump surfaces the nudges (pi.sendMessage at the boundary, mailbox.orchestrator_pump
# count>=1, notification.stale.suppressed ABSENT for goal keys); the scripted orchestrator
# then verifies the nudge is actionable + acks the lifecycle closed.
